Source: edison-image
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: open-edison <open-edison@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/open-edison/edison-image
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: edison-base
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libubootenv-tool, e2fsprogs, kmod, passwd, gpiod
Recommends: edison-firmware, linux-image-edison, bluez, apparmor
Description: Intel Edison (Kit for Arduino) system integration
 Services, tools and configuration for Debian on the Intel Edison: the
 Arduino kit's ACPI overlays and pin muxing, USB gadget networking and
 serial, settings that survive reflashing, the Arduino sketch service,
 the open-edison apt repository, and installing new kernels on the boot
 partition.

Package: edison-firmware
Architecture: all
Section: non-free-firmware/kernel
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, firmware-brcm80211
Description: Broadcom WiFi NVRAM and Bluetooth patch for the Intel Edison
 The Edison's calibration (NVRAM) file for its BCM43340 WiFi and the
 BCM43341B0 Bluetooth patch, from Intel's edison-firmware repository,
 redistributed unmodified under the Broadcom licence. Debian's
 firmware-brcm80211 provides the WiFi firmware itself.

Package: linux-image-edison
Architecture: amd64
Section: kernel
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, linux-image-${kernel:Release} (= ${kernel:Version})
Description: Linux kernel for the Intel Edison (meta package)
 Depends on the current kernel for the Edison, so that upgrading this
 package installs new kernel versions.
